  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Vedettes Îles d'Or &amp; Le Corsaire links Le Lavandou (year-round) as well as Cavalaire-sur-Mer and La Croix-Valmer (in season) to Port-Cros, Porquerolles and Le Levant. It's the most convenient option if you're based on this part of the Var coast rather than around Hyères.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Dogs on a lead are accepted free of charge on board the regular lines. The company itself sets out, in its own FAQ, the difference in rules between the islands: on <strong>Porquerolles</strong>, your dog can move around on a lead on the island, except on the main beaches during the day in summer. On <strong>Port-Cros</strong>, dogs are only allowed in the village (harbour area), specifically between Fort du Moulin and the Saint-Joseph statue, not on the island's trails — a point the company itself confirms. Certain specific excursions (the Seascope glass-bottom boat, longer wildlife outings) do not accept dogs: check at the time of booking. For category 1 and 2 dogs, a muzzle is required on board.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if you really want to walk with your dog, choose a simple crossing to Porquerolles rather than a themed excursion to Port-Cros — the "simple return trip" option is more flexible for dogs.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Le Lavandou and its long beach make a good stop before or after the crossing.</p>
